--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture (matches the established sibling W7 page AlertRulesPage)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- MVVM, no business logic in code-behind. The view binds AlertStudioPageViewModel and renders the
  pure AlertStudioDisplay projection; all branch selection / formatting / i18n happen in the headless
  Model/Projection. State changes are marshalled onto the UI thread (DispatcherQueue).
- Data port IAlertStudioFeed (the eleven web hooks) -> generated C# OpenAPI client (ADR-004):
    useAlertRules           -> get_api_v1_alerts_rules                 GET    /alerts/rules
    useNotificationChannels -> get_api_v1_notifications               GET    /notifications
    useVehicles             -> get_api_v1_vehicles                    GET    /vehicles
    useAlertMetrics         -> get_api_v1_alerts_metrics              GET    /alerts/metrics
    useSaveAlertRule        -> post_api_v1_alerts_rules               POST   /alerts/rules        (create)
                               put_api_v1_alerts_rules_ruleID         PUT    /alerts/rules/{id}   (update)
    useDeleteAlertRule      -> delete_api_v1_alerts_rules_ruleID      DELETE /alerts/rules/{id}
    useToggleAlertRule      -> put_api_v1_alerts_rules_ruleID         PUT    /alerts/rules/{id}   { enabled }
    useSnoozeAlertRule      -> post_api_v1_alerts_rules_ruleID_snooze POST   /alerts/rules/{id}/snooze { minutes }
    useTestAlertRule        -> post_api_v1_alerts_test                POST   /alerts/test
    useBulkEnableRules      -> post_api_v1_alerts_rules_bulk_enable   POST   /alerts/rules/bulk/enable  { ids }
    useBulkDisableRules     -> post_api_v1_alerts_rules_bulk_disable  POST   /alerts/rules/bulk/disable { ids }
  (all eleven operation ids cross-checked against apps/windows/Generated ApiEndpoints — all present.)
- Shared Fluent components reused (no web pixel-cloning, ADR-005/006): TsGlassPanel, PageTitle, Subhead,
  PanelTitle, Caption, Text, Label, ErrorText, TsButton, TsSelect, TsInput, TsToggle, TsCheckbox,
  TsSearchInput, TsBadge, TsSeverityBadge, TsStatusDot, TsEmptyState, TsErrorDisplay, TsSkeleton,
  TsAlertBanner, TsModal, and the BulkActionsToolbar shared surface (enable/disable + rule item-noun).
- i18n: every visible literal flows through ILocalizer.GetString("<key>","<English fallback>") via the
  single AlertStudioStrings.Resolve site (125 keyed calls). Per the established W7 contract the keys
  resolve through the WinUI resource bridge and fall back to the verbatim web English copy (sibling DONE
  pages add no resw rows; the keyed call site IS the resolution path). The headless test
  Resolve_requests_every_required_string_key asserts all 125 keys are requested (RecordingLocalizer),
  and Resolve_requests_exactly_125_keys pins the count.
- Units: this page has no SI-unit display fields (rule editor over raw signal names/operators); nothing
  is stored or computed non-SI. The numeric operands are opaque user-typed thresholds (web parity).
- Live data: the web page is TanStack queries only (no SSE source), so no >2min staleness chrome is
  applicable — matches the web source.
- The per-rule message body + the computed-metric operand are owned by the separately-gated W7 units
  AlertMessageEditor / ComputedMetricEditor; none of THIS unit's 125 strings belong to them, so the
  builder panel renders its own 125-string-bearing fields and the kind switch, faithfully reproducing
  the web region without duplicating those gated sub-units.

